WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.535
CHRIS HEMSWORTH
(VOICEOVER): I think

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.004
it's fair to say however
good we get at keeping humans

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.074
and sharks apart in
the ocean, there will

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.709
always be moments when we meet.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.112
[music playing]

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:17.016
And in those worst case
scenarios when sharks bite,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.653
is there anything
that can be done?

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.356
Charlie Huveneers is a
scientist who's thought

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.691
more about this than most.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.625
Hey, mate.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.826
How are you?

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.161
I'm not too bad, thanks.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.362
CHRIS HEMSWORTH (VOICEOVER):
For several years

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.064
he's been looking
at ways of deterring

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.700
sharks that decide to attack.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:38.605
Is your research and line
of work due to your passion

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.741
and love for sharks or
passionate and love for humans

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.309
or who are you--

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.944
who are you more invested in?

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.179
CHARLIE HUVENEERS: It depends--

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.515
It's OK to say sharks too.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.016
--it depends in
what situations.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.251
But, yeah, it's a combination.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.919
It's really I've
always been interested

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.087
in sharks since I'm a kid.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.588
Yeah.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.157
CHARLIE HUVENEERS: And, yeah,
the fascination for sharks

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.359
just turned into a
real inquest in--

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.594
into science and
understanding the sharks

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.296
better so that we
can actually help

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.332
in providing a safer
environment for some people

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.467
but also for sharks.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.535
Yeah.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.903
Are you going into
the field soon to test

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.204
any of those deterrents?

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.039
You know, actually we--
we're going next week.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.140
Well, good luck with it.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.208
CHARLIE HUVENEERS: Thanks.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.843
[music playing]

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.245
CHRIS HEMSWORTH (VOICEOVER):
Charlie and his colleagues

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.114
from Flinders
University in Adelaide

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.249
are heading into the
seas off South Australia.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.752
[music playing]

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.988
On board they're testing
the latest shark deterrent

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.691
and protection technologies.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.561
So what we've seen is
that in the recent years

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.497
there has been an increase
in the number of shark bite

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.566
globally, including
in Australia.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.837
And this has resulted in a
lot of interest in the devices

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.139
to try to reduce those risks.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.741
[water gurgling]

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.447
[long-nosed fur seal grunting]

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.082
CHRIS HEMSWORTH
(VOICEOVER): The team

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.984
have sailed to the
Neptune Islands, a hotspot

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.820
for great whites.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.389
The sharks come here to
prey on Australia's largest

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:06.192
colony of long-nosed fur seals.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.927
[long-nosed fur seal grunting]

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.362
So it's the perfect
place to test

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.464
products designed
to take advantage

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:14.934
of sharks' very unusual senses.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:18.071
There's only a small number of
animals that have this ability

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.540
to detect electric
field and sharks

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.843
have it through these black dots
called ampullae of Lorenzini.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.380
The idea behind this electric
field-based deterrent

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:31.017
is that they will produce such
a strong pulse that it will

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:35.855
overwhelm the sensory organ
and make the shark basically

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.358
move away from the source.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.759
CHRIS HEMSWORTH
(VOICEOVER): The aim

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:43.730
is to develop a safer surfboard
with an electrical shark

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.399
deterrent built into it.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:49.235
This produces
an electric field

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.739
through two electrodes
which are positioned

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.873
just underneath the board.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.576
And this is, kind of, a
replica of a surfboard.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.145
This has produced a field
which is transmitted

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:01.381
to this electrode
and creates a bit

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.884
of a barrier around the
surfboard, which in theory

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.619
should be deterring the sharks.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.288
[music playing]

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.657
CHRIS HEMSWORTH (VOICEOVER):
To test the theory,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.092
the experiment compares
a sharks reactions

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.328
to a board with the
electrical device switched

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.830
on to a board with it off.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.099
[music playing]

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.236
But getting robust
data means repeating

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.471
the process many times over.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.107
[music playing]

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.749
Over hundreds of
previous trials,

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.851
the team have captured
remarkable footage

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.820
of sharks in action.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:41.888
[commotion]

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.160
First they recorded what
happened to a baited board

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.529
with the device turned off.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.297
It's interesting
that we do have a bait

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.599
just underneath that board.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.434
WOMAN: It's swimming as
we would expect to see

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.135
it swimming around the bait.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.671
[music playing]

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.642
CHRIS HEMSWORTH
(VOICEOVER): And then

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.678
what happened to the sharks
when the device was turned on?

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.682
OK.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.352
So that was a
pretty obvious flinch.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.555
CHARLIE HUVENEERS:
He's coming back now.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:18.758
That kind of flinch or reaction,
we didn't see that when

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.093
the deterrent was turned off.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.562
[music playing]

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.365
WOMAN: And you
can see the really

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:29.102
obvious flinching in the gills
as well and the jaw gaping.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.604
[music playing]

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.240
CHARLIE HUVENEERS:
Wow, look at that one.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.708
So that one came really from
down below and it was only

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:39.045
within half a meter.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.681
Overall there was
a 60% reduction

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.349
in the proportion
of bait being taken,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.618
so a 60% reduction
in shark bites.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.820
[music playing]

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.223
CHRIS HEMSWORTH (VOICEOVER):
If the eight people killed

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.525
by sharks in
Australia in 2020 had

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.461
been able to use an electric
deterrent like this,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.697
then five may still be alive.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.233
[music playing]

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.504
Products like
these are promising

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:08.107
as we may be able to reduce
fatalities in the future

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.876
or without harming the sharks.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:16.349
[music playing]

